pocketchip-batt (0.4) trixie; urgency=low

  * warn05/warn15: replace the unbounded busy-loop that read voltage with a
    single read + safe-high default (3700). On an empty/missing voltage file the
    old `while [ -z "$VOLT" ]` loop never exited, so the oneshot warn services
    spun until systemd's start-timeout and were marked FAILED.
  * warn05/warn15 + warn-clean.service: `rm` -> `rm -f` so removing an absent
    flag file (the common case) no longer fails the unit; added a trailing
    `exit 0` to the warn scripts.
  * pocketchip-batt poller: validate the bc result and write voltage atomically
    (temp + mv) so it never leaves an empty voltage file for the warn readers.

 -- Ben Young <computermouth@proton.me>  Thu, 18 Jun 2026 02:30:00 -0500

